    "answer": {
      "short": "He divided by the selling price instead of the cost price. The correct percentage profit is $25\\%$.",
      "worked": "Percentage profit is calculated using the original cost price, $\\$12$, as the denominator, rather than the selling price, $\\$15$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Profit} &= \\$15-\\$12\\\\\\text{Profit} &= \\$3\\\\\\text{Percentage profit} &= \\frac{3}{12}\\times100\\%\\\\\\text{Percentage profit} &= 25\\%\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 24
